 {:id "adr-2607078000-kotoba-lang-wasm-webcomponent-cljs-esm-host"
  :title "ADR-2607078000: wasm-webcomponent's zero-build-step hand-JS host policy is superseded — kotoba/kototama WASM hosts are authored in ClojureScript, compiled once, run everywhere (browser + Node)"
  :status "accepted"
  :date "2026-07-07"
  :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"]
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kotoba-lang-wasm-webcomponent-cljs-esm-host"
  :authoritative true
  :authoritative_for
  ["kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent: new policy -- kotoba/kototama WASM hosts needing more than a trivial hand-port are authored in ClojureScript and compiled via shadow-cljs :target :esm to a single ES module that runs identically in browser and Node, instead of hand-written per-platform JS. Existing hand-JS modules (actor-host.js/kgraph.js/has-capability.js/kotoba-wasm-element.js) are grandfathered, not retrofitted."
   "kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent src-cljs/kotoba/kami_engine_host.cljs (+ shadow-cljs.edn, compiled src/kami-engine-host.js, test/verify-kami-engine-host.mjs, examples/kami-engine-host/): first implementation under the new policy -- 1:1 port of kami-script-runtime-rs's HostState/EcsStore/KamiHost (14 kami:engine/* host-imports across 4 WASM import modules), parity-verified in Node against the real isekai-network-01-netsurvivors.wasm fixture for 300 ticks (entities=16 shiro-pico=1 ghost=14 beat-spark=1, exact match with kami-script-runtime-rs's own documented Rust/wasmtime trace)."
   "clojurewasm (cljw) ruled out for WASM-host-providing-imports roles: (1) native-binary-only, does not run in a browser; (2) its WebAssembly FFI is Clojure-calls-wasm only (wasm/load + wasm/call), no documented capability for cljw to provide host-import functions a guest wasm module calls into. Verified via its own README, not assumed."
   "Addendum 2026-07-08: direction widened to Rust-free including native/windowed targets, not just browser/Node. Concurrent-session work on kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs (wasmi backend + kami_clj_play native winit+wgpu player) left untouched/unreverted (real, verified, another session's in-progress work), but a documentation-only org-direction notice was added to that crate's README.md/Cargo.toml (commit 4f08f5b42ae7bd4ac0ff91ab0e9c0f80e1b0c068) recording that native desktop targets should go through a webview/Chromium-shell wrapper around the same kami-engine-host/dom-gpu ClojureScript path going forward, not hand-written wgpu/winit. KamiHost's headless-host role (this ADR's actual replacement target, src/lib.rs) verified unaffected by the concurrent session's additions."]
